  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on variance, preferring higher variance. The individual, however, discusses expected payout and the value of a secure outcome—indicating sensitivity to risk and possibly using expected value as a criterion. They favor the sure outcome (Lottery B), which has zero variance, while the variance-based reason would favor Lottery A (higher variance). The individual does not mention variability, spread, or any concept related to variance. Instead, they emphasize security and expected value. Therefore, the information considered (expected value, certainty) does not align with the variance-based reason, and their justification (preference for safety) contradicts the rule of preferring higher variance. There is no indication that variance was part of their deliberation.",
